// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_win_reg_write_protect_for_storage_disabled.yml
// ID Sigma: 75f7a0e2-7154-4c4d-9eae-5cdb4e0a5c13
// Título: Write Protect For Storage Disabled
// Descripción: Detects applications trying to modify the registry in order to disable any write-protect property for storage devices.
This could be a precursor to a ransomware attack and has been an observed technique used by cypherpunk group.

// Fecha de creación: 2021-06-11
// Fecha de modificación: 2024-01-18
// Aplica a: Producto: windows | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: windows
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: medium
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\windows\process_creation\proc_creation_win_reg_write_protect_for_storage_disabled.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control" and ProcessCommandLine contains "Write Protection" and ProcessCommandLine contains "0" and ProcessCommandLine contains "storage"
